    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d378">

                <pb facs="0505" n="420" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg420"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.94/312</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Japanese Appointed Ambassador</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Shidehara</hi>)</head>
                <p>The Secretary of State presents his compliments to His Excellency the Japanese
                    Ambassador and has the honor to acknowledge the receipt of his memorandum of
                    December 13, 1919, with enclosure, regarding the question of the so-called
                    “picture brides.”</p>
                <p>The Secretary of State avails himself of this opportunity to express the
                    appreciation with which the Government of the United States has noted the action
                    thus taken by the Imperial Japanese Government. It is confidently hoped that
                    this action will remove a source of misunderstanding between the two peoples and
                    serve to maintain their relations upon a basis of good understanding.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1919-12-27">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 27, 1919</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
